  "checks": [
    "The real users API creates a separate account with isPlatformAdmin:false and an explicit local BUILDING_ADMIN membership. One exact-ID owner fixture INSERT grants its global PLATFORM_ADMIN binding with 2s lock and 3s statement limits; readback confirms flag false, local role and effective global/MFA authority. No account flag, factor or session proof is written by the fixture.",
    "The UI login retains the legacy BUILDING_ADMIN role while returning enrollment-required and empty operational memberships. The required gate is visible, navigation is absent and the protected building GET denies with MFA_ENROLLMENT_REQUIRED.",
    "Real UI enrollment and TOTP confirmation return ten unique recovery codes; Close and Escape cannot dismiss the held ceremony, while its original UI bearer already reports satisfied at the server.",
    "No page-originated non-auth API request is observed before the response event for a GET/auth/me initiated after acknowledgment is armed. That response body is then separately checked for the same identity, satisfied state and explicit membership.",
    "After acknowledgment the page requests buildings, navigation becomes visible, saved codes leave the DOM, and direct reads using the original UI bearer prove the correct building plus units:manage and teams:manage capabilities.",
    "The required settings UI offers no disable button. A direct real HTTP disable attempt with the same proven UI bearer denies 403/MFA_REQUIRED and preserves the enabled factor, ten unused recovery codes and satisfied session state."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The initial proof verifier was blocked by the long Windows screenshot path after runtime success. This V2 changes only evidence-path IO; it preserves the prior verifier and all runtime/media metadata and does not rerun any test.",
    "Exactly one independent global-binding required-MFA administrator case is accepted; the prior flag-based case, three-case browser and renderer results remain separate evidence and are not added here.",
    "Only an active global PLATFORM_ADMIN binding with legacy flag false and one explicit local BUILDING_ADMIN membership is exercised. This does not cover inactive/expired/catalog-disabled bindings, support users, live promotion/revocation races, all authority combinations or a second family requiring verification.",
    "Account and local membership setup use real HTTP; global authority setup is one authorized owner-SQL fixture INSERT because this source has no public route for global PLATFORM_ADMIN grants. It is not a 100 percent HTTP setup, an authorization mock or a direct MFA/session-proof write. The official UUID lifecycle owns final cleanup.",
    "The network oracle is page.on(request), excluding separate APIRequestContext setup/assertion calls. Its boundary is the 200 response event/headers for the post-arming acknowledgment GET/me, with body identity checked afterward; it is not internal provider-mount instrumentation or universal request/parsing linearization.",
    "One Chromium worker and zero retries; no Firefox/WebKit matrix, Android, iOS, device, Codegen, full webapp or load acceptance.",
    "This increment executes E2E types and one-case listing. The prior V4 building type result is reused only because all product sources and its config match exactly; no new building type execution is claimed.",
    "A QA-only ESM startup entrypoint invokes the same application, restricted-role checks and event bus, then binds 127.0.0.1; the product server.ts is preserved.",
    "The frontend consumer is freshly built in production mode; API and fixture execute with NODE_ENV=test on a disposable UUID database.",
    "Visual review means the final screenshot and three sampled video frames, not watching every frame or asserting exhaustive UX coverage.",
    "The raw MFA video remains private because the scenario displays ephemeral factor/recovery material. No public video is eligible from this run; publication of a reviewed final screenshot is a separate root action.",
    "The 2048 MiB memory requirement is a phase/startup guard, including the observation after API/preview startup. Heartbeats during the browser run are measurements, not a continuous 2048 MiB acceptance threshold.",
    "No performance conclusion, production readiness, deployment, migration publication, commit or push is performed by this verifier."
  ],
